ecutable specs beside the markdown — sumcheck, superspartan (outer and inner sumcheck over CCS), the HyperNova fold step and the decider's algebraic part. The PCS is an oracle in these files (an `instance` evaluation), which is how IOPs are analysed anyway; the lens's own soundness stays with the lens.\n  * a CI job on zippel's pinned nightly toolchain, separate from the stable workspace: `cargo zcheck` on every file, then completeness and special soundness at small sizes. The release-train gate for zheng includes it.\n  * a Goldilocks analysis backend contributed upstream, so sized-type checks (degree against field size) run in our field.\n  * diff the derived transcript against transcript: every disagreement is either a spec bug or a doc bug.\n\nNot: replacing zheng's prover or verifier with zippel's runtime (arkworks, big fields, CPU only, no hash-based commitments), and not a dependency in any soft3 crate.\n\n## first experiment — done 2026-10-24\n\nThe IOP of `rs/src/spartan` + `rs/src/sumcheck` is in `specs/proto/` as five zippel protocols; results in audit/zippel-2026-10-24. The whole IOP (CCS fixed, lens as oracle) is complete by the Gröbner analysis in 43 ms; the outer and inner sumchecks alone pass up to three and four variables; a deliberate bug (a degree-3 round polynomial sent as three points) type-checks and runs but fails completeness in 4.5 s; the derived transcript order matches `transcript.rs`. Special soundness does not apply in the oracle model (no witness, nothing to extract), so a soundness verdict needs the commitment inside the protocol, which the hash-based lens cannot give zippel today. The gate to keep: `zippel-check` + completeness at those sizes + the bug variant failing.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nsp1-gpu-jagged-assist 6.8.1 - Docs.rs (https://docs.rs/crate/sp1-gpu-jagged-assist/6.8.1)\nciteturn6search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; # sp1-gpu-jagged-as